5
00:00:54.635 --> 00:01:16.912
So, here we go. It is the final session. Be reminded. Remember, my brothers, over and over in the scriptures, it says to be reminded and keep on remembering. And today, that is what we are going to do is be reminded.

6
00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:32.382
Confused men create major problems and confused men settle for less. The Bible has answers and insights so that we can be unstuck and not be confused.

7
00:01:32.382 --> 00:01:46.717
Many of us have a father wound. We express it in anger or we suppress it in obsession and addiction or we stay lost and stuck and confused.

8
00:01:46.717 --> 00:02:13.531
And what we needed from our fathers, what each son needs from his father is positive memories, direction, conviction that comes through modeling that we see that he knows what to do and is doing it and is not just saying it and that we have his father's heart.

9
00:02:13.531 --> 00:02:34.879
That is what sons need and as fathers we need to be providing. As we have these father wounds, we know there are remedies for them. And the first one is to conjure up, summon the courage to forgive our dads.

10
00:02:34.879 --> 00:02:54.887
We would risk asking for his love, who would re-aggressively seek reconciliation with him. We would risk asking for his blessing. And we would enter into the greater Father's love. So important.

11
00:02:54.887 --> 00:03:05.819
And then we would break the cycle as being dads and break that cycle becoming a responsible dad ourselves.

12
00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:21.289
Coupled with an absent father is the overly bonded mother wound. It is typical when a son grows up mainly under the supervision or direction of women.

13
00:03:21.289 --> 00:03:40.781
Results in ourselves in either rebelling against women and becoming dominant towards them or overly identifying with women. Behaving and reacting in ways that are more appropriate to women.

14
00:03:40.781 --> 00:04:06.977
The remedies for the overly bonded mother wound is to find masculine focus as many of us have done in this course in this study, to establish masculine boundaries and to establish strong relationships with men which we are calling you to in these groups.

15
00:04:06.977 --> 00:04:26.675
So as fathers, a key thing that we do is we call our sons in adolescence away from mom and into manhood. We do that with a direct call. It is specific. We give them a cause beyond themselves.

16
00:04:26.675 --> 00:04:40.288
What Tim would say is a transcendent cause, a masculine vision of manhood, a code of conduct, and that all culminates in a ceremony.

17
00:04:40.288 --> 00:05:05.452
And that those last four things, a cause beyond themselves, a masculine vision of manhood, and a code of conduct culminating in a ceremony is my plug for Journey to Manhood, which is the next four Wednesdays right here in this room at 6:30 a.m.

18
00:05:05.452 --> 00:05:28.863
If you have a son 11 to 15, I would say do everything you can to be in that training and then take the next 9 to 12 months with a group of men that have done that into a ceremony and a year-long vision of manhood for your sons.

19
00:05:28.863 --> 00:05:37.113
If your son is older than that and you have not done that, it is never too late.

20
00:05:37.113 --> 00:05:47.117
And none of this is done alone. It is never in isolation. Strong community with men is essential.

21
00:05:47.117 --> 00:06:09.084
Without strong community with men, we know that we have no accountability and we allow things in our life that we would not otherwise allow. We do not have cheerleaders. Men, we need motivation when it gets tough.

22
00:06:09.084 --> 00:06:29.298
We do not have intimacy. We become plastic versions of ourselves that are not transparent and we begin to put on masks and hide. And there is no challenge. We stay stuck in an earthly perspective.

23
00:06:29.298 --> 00:06:48.584
It is the reason we need strong community with men. It is essential in our lives. As you are seeking out this community of men, you find men that support you rather than compete with you.

24
00:06:48.584 --> 00:07:08.488
Who are your cheerleader and not your critic, that help you develop your gifts, that encourage you while protecting you from costly mistakes, and who recognize, value, and see potential in you.

25
00:07:08.488 --> 00:07:22.823
Those are the kinds of men we are looking for in strong community. Those are the type of men I hope you found in your groups this semester.

26
00:07:22.823 --> 00:07:42.624
Because we have a depravity wound. We were born in a fallen Adam nature, cursed creatures at odds with God. In this depravity, we were separated from God. We are subject to a life of futility.

27
00:07:42.624 --> 00:08:04.075
